    /// <summary>The ONE §4.2.6/§4.2.7/§4.2.13 non-support emit shape (the COBOLNET1560 band): NAME the
    /// facility on the non-failing warning channel, then bind to a no-op. Never a parallel Unsupported()
    /// method on EditionContext — Edition.Warning is the single writer (feedback_singular_pattern).</summary>
    private BoundStatement BindUnsupportedFacility(
        DiagnosticDescriptor d, string facility, string disposition, string effect)
    {
        Ctx.Edition.Warning(d.Code,
            $"{facility} is {disposition} that is not supported — it is accepted but produces no {effect}; "
            + "the remainder of the sentence is consumed (see docs/CONFORMANCE.md §4)");
        return new BoundNop();
    }

The trailing '; the remainder of the sentence is consumed' clause is REQUIRED, not cosmetic: the (~DOT)* swallow greedily absorbs any statement that follows the facility verb in the same sentence, and silently dropping a valid statement without saying so would be a silent wrong answer. §4.2.6 excuses diagnosing the unsupported syntax; it does not excuse concealing the consumption. Confirm the exact accessor names (`Ctx.Edition` vs `Edition`) against the surrounding arms before writing — the file's other arms delegate to sub-binders.

