grammarChanges.newText:
// VALUE Clause — IS is optional noise word.
// Format 2 (table, §13.18.63.2): {VALUE IS|VALUES ARE} {{literal-1}... FROM (subscript-1...) [TO (subscript-2...)]}...
//   The FROM/TO subscript lists lex in DEFAULT mode: FROM and TO are hard reserved words, absent from
//   cobol-words.json's subscriptTrigger set, so OnDefaultLParen does NOT push SUBSCRIPT mode.
// Formats 1/3/4/5 keep the historical arm. Alternative ORDER: the table arm is FIRST and is disambiguated
// solely by the mandatory FROM keyword after the literal list — it cannot shadow the bare-list arm.
// The valueItem/operand loop guard: at 2002+ PROPERTY is reserved (ISO 8.9) so it can NEVER be a
// constant-name operand — without the predicate the greedy loop consumes it as a cobolWord and the
// propertyClause (13.18.42) that follows VALUE never matches. At 85 PROPERTY stays a legal user word.
valueClause
    : (VALUE | VALUES) (IS | ARE)? valueClauseTablePhrase+
    | (VALUE | VALUES) (IS | ARE)? valueItem ({!(is2002() && TokenStream.LA(1)==PROPERTY)}? COMMA? valueItem)*
      (WHEN SET TO FALSE_ IS? literal)?
      (IN IDENTIFIER)?
    ;

// One `{literal-1}... FROM (subscript-1...) [TO (subscript-2...)]` phrase of a Format-2 VALUE clause
// (§13.18.63.2 Format 2). The clause repeats the whole phrase (the outer `+` on valueClause), and GR15
// makes a LATER phrase overwrite an earlier one for the same element. subscript-1/subscript-2 are integer
// numeric literals (SR19) — the parser accepts integerLiteral and the binder enforces >= 1 and the SR20/21
// count/range/order rules, which need the resolved OCCURS chain.
valueClauseTablePhrase
    : valueClauseOperand ({!(is2002() && TokenStream.LA(1)==PROPERTY)}? COMMA? valueClauseOperand)*
      FROM LPAREN integerLiteral (COMMA? integerLiteral)* RPAREN
      (TO LPAREN integerLiteral (COMMA? integerLiteral)* RPAREN)?
    ;

// valueClause is SHARED: data-description entries (13.16 fmt 1 -> VALUE fmt 1/2), level-88 entries
// (fmt 3 / fmt 5), report-group entries (fmt 4) and screen entries (fmt 1, SR15). Any gate or check keyed
// on this rule MUST positively guard its section (DEVLOG 736) — see VersionConformancePass.InGatedDataEntry.

